---
import HeroViewer from './HeroViewer.svelte';
---
<section class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl items-start gap-12 px-5 pb-20 pt-32 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_minmax(0,1.2fr)] lg:gap-14 lg:pt-40">
  <div>
    <p class="label">Pre-release · built in Rust · phases 1–5 of 6</p>
    <h1 class="display mt-5 text-[clamp(2.25rem,4.2vw,3.5rem)]">
      Sketch, machine, simulate and route in one program.
    </h1>
    <p class="lead mt-6">
      Kerfwright is a CAD, CAM, FEA and ECAD suite on its own B-rep kernel. The sketches, the parametric history, the
      toolpaths, the studies and the board all live in one <code class="font-mono text-[.9em]">.kwf</code> file, so a
      change to a dimension reaches the G-code.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-9 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
      <a href="/docs/getting-started/build-from-source/" class="btn btn-primary">Build from source</a>
      <a href="/docs/getting-started/introduction/" class="btn btn-quiet">Read the documentation</a>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8 max-w-md">
      <p class="mb-2 text-[.9375rem] text-soft">There are no installers yet. With Rust and a Vulkan, Metal or DX12 GPU:</p>
      <div class="code flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <code id="run-cmd">cargo run --release -p kw-app</code>
        <button type="button" id="copy-cmd" class="min-h-9 shrink-0 rounded px-2 text-[.8125rem] text-soft hover:bg-paper hover:text-ink" aria-label="Copy command">Copy</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div>
    <HeroViewer client:idle />
  </div>
</section>
<script>
  const b = document.getElementById('copy-cmd');
  b?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    try {
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.getElementById('run-cmd')!.textContent ?? '');
      b.textContent = 'Copied';
      setTimeout(() => (b.textContent = 'Copy'), 1600);
    } catch { b.textContent = 'Press Ctrl+C'; }
  });
</script>
